{
  "action": "In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
  "description": "USN-8972-1 fixed vulnerabilities in HAProxy. On Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, the\nupdate caused a regression when processing certain chunked requests. This\nupdate fixes the problem.\n\nWe apologize for the inconvenience.\n\nOriginal advisory details:\n\n It was discovered that HAProxy incorrectly handled truncated HTTP/2\n PING frames. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause\n HAProxy to consume excessive CPU resources, leading to a denial of\n service. (CVE-2026-110353)\n\n It was discovered that HAProxy incorrectly handled certain HTTP/1.1\n chunked requests. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to\n cause HAProxy to consume excessive CPU resources, leading to a denial\n of service. (CVE-2026-110354)",
